course: dictionary
lesson: 9984
title: Teatime and the words around it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Teatime is a noun for a time of day. In British, Irish, Australian and New Zealand homes, «tea» can mean the evening meal, so teatime is dinner time, often around 5 or 6 pm. Read the words around it to work out which time is meant.
explain: «Nana is 68 and gets tired by teatime.» The word tired tells you the day is getting long, and by teatime means by the time of the evening meal, late in the day. Swap your meaning into the sentence: «Nana gets tired by dinner time» still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: «The knock came at teatime.» The words came at tell you teatime is a moment in time, not a drink or a food. Teatime can also be used in phrases such as «at teatime», «by teatime» and «teatime treat». In the UK it can also mean the afternoon time for a cup of tea, so check the clues to see which one the writer means.
fact: Teatime is a noun, and it names a time of day.
fact: In British, Irish, Australian and New Zealand homes, «tea» can mean the evening meal.
fact: «Teatime» usually means dinner time, often around 5 or 6 pm.
fact: In the UK, «teatime» can also mean the afternoon time for a cup of tea with cake or biscuits.
fact: Useful phrases: «at teatime», «by teatime» and «teatime treat».
exercise: «Nana is 68 and gets tired by teatime.» What does teatime mean here? | The time at night when people go to bed | The time in the morning when people wake up | *The time in the early evening when people eat their evening meal
exercise: «The knock came at teatime.» Which words could replace teatime? | midnight | *dinner time | sunrise
exercise: In «Nana gets tired by teatime», what does by mean? | at breakfast | only on Sundays | *before or when teatime comes | after bedtime
test: In the UK, teatime can also mean what, in the afternoon? | a thunderstorm | a school sports day | *a cup of tea with cake or biscuits
test: Which phrase from the lesson shows teatime is a time? | cup of tea | tea towel | *at teatime
exam: Which of these is a «teatime treat»? | a school bus | *a slice of cake | a pair of muddy boots | a sleeping bag
